{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ProofHygiene.SelfAssumingContexts","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.SelfAssumingContexts","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.separation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.separation","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L245-L257","doc":"**The separation.** At `H = C = False` the conditional class is inhabited and the\ndecoy class is not. Same conclusion, opposite inhabitedness — so the two shapes are\ngenuinely different objects, and \"carries the implication\" versus \"carries the\nimplication *and asserts its antecedent*\" is a real distinction rather than a stylistic\npreference.\n\nThis is what makes `proof-decoy-hypothesis` a criterion: a reviewer can ask whether the\nclass supplies its own antecedent, and that question has a definite answer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.conditional_not_contentless","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.conditional_not_contentless","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L238-L243","doc":"**A genuine conditional class is NOT contentless for the conclusion**, witnessed at\n`H = C = False` — it is inhabited there while the conclusion fails. This is the reviewer's\ntest (`not_contentless_of_witness`) run on the shape that should pass it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.conditional_nonempty_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.conditional_nonempty_iff","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L230-L236","doc":"A conditional class is inhabited iff the implication holds — **weaker** than `C`, and\nexactly what \"conditional on `H`\" ought to mean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.ConditionalContext.impl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.ConditionalContext.impl","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L228-L228","doc":"The implication only. The antecedent `H` is the consumer's to supply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.ConditionalContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.ConditionalContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L226-L226","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.ConditionalContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.ConditionalContext","kind":"structure","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L224-L228","doc":"**A genuine conditional class** (§3b-cond): it carries the implication and leaves the\nantecedent to the consumer. Note what is absent — there is no `H` field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.decoy_of_false_not_inhabited","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.decoy_of_false_not_inhabited","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L218-L222","doc":"**The pattern is not universally inhabited** — which is exactly why it looks like it\nsays something. At `C = False` no decoy context exists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.decoy_premise_irrelevant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.decoy_premise_irrelevant","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L211-L216","doc":"**The named premise carries no logical weight.** Given the conclusion, a decoy context\nexists with premise `True` — so `bloch_suslin`, `peter_weyl_holds` and the rest are decor.\nThe apparent content of these declarations lives in the *name*, not in the Lean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.decoy_contentless","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.decoy_contentless","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L206-L209","doc":"The decoy shape in the criterion's vocabulary: contentless, like the projection and\ntuple shapes, despite extracting its conclusion by application rather than projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.decoy_nonempty_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.decoy_nonempty_iff","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L194-L204","doc":"**The decoy class is inhabited exactly when its conclusion holds.**\n\nSo writing the class and instantiating it is logically identical to assuming `C`. The\nforward direction is the pattern's own theorem; the backward direction takes the premise\nto be `True`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.decoy_conclusion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.decoy_conclusion","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L189-L192","doc":"The pattern's \"theorem\": an **application**, not a projection, which is why a\nfield-projection scan cannot see it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.DecoyContext.impl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.DecoyContext.impl","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L187-L187","doc":"…and an implication into the conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.DecoyContext.premise_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.DecoyContext.premise_holds","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L185-L185","doc":"…asserted to hold, which is the step that makes the class equivalent to `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.DecoyContext.premise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.DecoyContext.premise","kind":"def","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L183-L183","doc":"The named premise — `bloch_suslin`, `acoustic_horizon_formed`, … ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.DecoyContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.DecoyContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L181-L181","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.DecoyContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.DecoyContext","kind":"structure","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L176-L187","doc":"**The decoy-hypothesis shape.** A named premise, an assertion that it holds, and an\nimplication into the conclusion. This is the shape of `B1TorusKnotRowsContext`,\n`AcousticHorizonConditionsContext`, `DiscreteVortexSpectrumContext`,\n`KelvinDispersionDerivationContext`, `QOUFluidUniverse`, `QuantumPeterWeylContext` and\nthe rest of the `proof-decoy-hypothesis` cluster, with the names abstracted away. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.tuple_contentless","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.tuple_contentless","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L171-L174","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.TupleContext.snd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.TupleContext.snd","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L169-L169","doc":"Second conclusion, likewise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.TupleContext.fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.TupleContext.fst","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L167-L167","doc":"First conclusion, carried as a hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.TupleContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.TupleContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L165-L165","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.TupleContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.TupleContext","kind":"structure","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L161-L169","doc":"**The tuple shape**: several conclusions bundled, the \"theorem\" projecting one out.\nThis is `proof-tuple-projection`. Bundling does not dilute the defect — the class is\ninhabited iff *both* hold, so it is contentless for the conjunction, and projecting either\ncomponent is still assuming it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.selfAssuming_contentless","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.selfAssuming_contentless","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L156-L159","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.SelfAssumingContext.claim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.SelfAssumingContext.claim","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L154-L154","doc":"The conclusion, carried as a hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.SelfAssumingContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.SelfAssumingContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L152-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.SelfAssumingContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.SelfAssumingContext","kind":"structure","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L148-L154","doc":"**The bluntest shape: a field of the conclusion's own type**, with the \"theorem\"\n`ctx.claim`. This is `proof-field-projection` / `exact-field-projection`, and it is what\nAGENTS.md §3b-cond item 5 calls a *\"vacuous self-assuming projection\"* — stated there in\nprose, machine-checked here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.not_contentless_of_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.not_contentless_of_witness","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L140-L146","doc":"**The reviewer's test.** If the class can be instantiated while the conclusion fails,\nit is not contentless — it carries something. Contrapositively, a class you can only\ninstantiate by already having `C` proves nothing about `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProofHygiene.Contentless","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProofHygiene.Contentless","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ProofHygiene/SelfAssumingContexts.lean#L108-L116","doc":"**A context class is contentless for `C` when it is inhabited exactly when `C` holds.**\n\nInstantiating such a class is then logically identical to assuming `C`, whatever the\nclass's fields are named and however the conclusion is extracted from them — by a\nprojection, by an application, or by a chain of either.\n\nThe negation is the practical test, and it is the one a reviewer can actually run:\n**exhibit an instance without already having the conclusion** (`not_contentless_of_witness`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}